+/*
+ * Samsara port: inert implementation of the input-method proxy.
+ *
+ * The reasoning is in improxy.h; this file is what makes the stub true. There
+ * is exactly one thing to get right here, and it is not the constructor.
+ *
+ * The constructor must leave the object with no descriptor. `setFd(-1)` is what
+ * makes fd() report -1, and fd() is what the io dispatcher uses to decide
+ * whether this object has anything to wait on. If a descriptor were installed,
+ * the dispatcher would select() on it, it would never become readable, and the
+ * terminal would sit in select() forever with the shell already running and
+ * nothing ever typed -- a hang with no diagnostic, which is the worst shape a
+ * failure can take.
+ *
+ * So: no socketpair, no fork, no descriptor, and actived() false so no
+ * keystroke is ever routed here. The result is that this object costs a
+ * construction and a deletion and does nothing, which is exactly what "feature
+ * unavailable" should cost.
+ */
+
